+\AuthorResponse{We thank the reviewer for this suggestion. The original study used predictors from the same local 25-cell domain as the regional-mean target and therefore did not explicitly incorporate atmospheric conditions farther upstream to the west. In existing matched refits (same split, window, hyperparameters, training-only scaling, five seeds and test targets), the pre-specified configuration C3 added a western near-upstream box (U1: 52.75--53.75$^\circ$N, 10.5--7.0$^\circ$W; the seven original variables plus wind speed) and an Atlantic box (U2: 50--57$^\circ$N, 20--7$^\circ$W; 500-hPa geopotential and tcwv). RMSE decreased by 6.4\% for XGBoost and 7.0\% for BiLSTM-Attention, with all five seeds improving and both seed-t and moving-block intervals excluding zero; wet and upper-tail errors also decreased (Supplementary Tables~\ref{supp-stab:r2m3_upstream_xgboost} and~\ref{supp-stab:r2m3_upstream_bilstm_attn}). Because C3 adds variables and spatial coverage together, it does not isolate the effect of domain extension alone. Exploratory single-box and incremental refits (Supplementary Table~\ref{supp-stab:r3d_upstream_increments} and Fig.~\ref{supp-sfig:r3d_upstream_effects}) indicate that U1 provided most of the gain for XGBoost, whereas adding U2 to U1 reduced BiLSTM-Attention RMSE by a further 1.7\%. The boxes were fixed in advance rather than optimized, only two models and the main split were tested, and the inputs are ERA5 reanalysis fields, so no optimal domain is claimed. For weekly mean subseasonal predictions, \citet[Section~5a]{goutham2023statistical} found that restricting the predictor domain to the predictand domain degraded skill; we cite this in Section~\ref{manuscript-sec:limitations} as context, not as validation of our boxes or of six-hour precipitation prediction.}
+
+\ManuscriptChange{Section~\ref{manuscript-sec:limitations} (Limitations and Future Work): new paragraph after the feature-selection limitation, citing \citet{goutham2023statistical} (added to the reference list). Supplementary Material: new final section ``Upstream predictor domain'' with Table~\ref{supp-stab:r3d_upstream_increments} and Fig.~\ref{supp-sfig:r3d_upstream_effects} (C3 vs C3a and C3 vs C3b). The C3/C3a/C3b comparisons with C0 remain those in Section~\ref{manuscript-sec:predictor_complementarity} and Supplementary Tables~\ref{supp-stab:r2m3_upstream_xgboost} and~\ref{supp-stab:r2m3_upstream_bilstm_attn}, unchanged; no training or data download. Final page and line numbers pending full-manuscript assembly.}
+
+\EvidenceBox{Local predictor domain and upstream inputs (Section~\ref{manuscript-sec:limitations})}{
+\RevisedExcerpt{The original predictors were restricted to the local 25-cell domain and therefore did not explicitly incorporate atmospheric conditions farther upstream to the west. The C3 gains reported in Section~\ref{sec:predictor_complementarity} were consistent across all five seeds, with both seed-t and moving-block intervals excluding zero (Supplementary Tables~\ref{supp-stab:r2m3_upstream_xgboost} and~\ref{supp-stab:r2m3_upstream_bilstm_attn}). Because C3 added variables and spatial coverage together, it does not isolate the effect of extending the domain alone. In the exploratory comparisons, the western near-upstream box (U1) accounted for most of the gain for XGBoost, whereas adding the Atlantic box (U2) to U1 further reduced BiLSTM-Attention RMSE (Supplementary Table~\ref{supp-stab:r3d_upstream_increments} and Fig.~\ref{supp-sfig:r3d_upstream_effects}). In subseasonal downscaling of weekly mean fields, \citet{goutham2023statistical} found that restricting the predictor domain to the predictand domain considerably degraded prediction quality, whereas shifting a predictand-sized domain westward did not improve on a centred one; this provides context rather than validation of six-hour precipitation prediction or of the present boxes. The upstream boxes were fixed before the refits and were not optimized, and only two models, the main chronological split and ERA5 reanalysis inputs were tested; no optimal predictor domain is therefore identified.}
+}
 
